# mesh_patterns: 3D mesh -> flat panels by LSCM -> SVG and PDF patterns at 1:1 scale.

# --- structure
The program "mesh_patterns" contains the module "main", the module "loader", the window "viewer", the module "flattener", the module "distortion" and the module "exporter".
The module "loader" contains the mesh "mesh".
The window "viewer" contains the state machine "seam mode", the list "seam_edges", the stack "seam_segments", the graph "edge graph", the list "panels" and the state machine "distortion mode".
The module "flattener" contains the function "segment_by_seams", the function "cut_to_disk", the algorithm "lscm" and the function "flatten_patch".
The module "distortion" contains the function "compute_distortion" and the percentile "angular p95".
The module "exporter" contains the function "export_svg" and the function "export_pdf".

# --- relations
The module "main" uses the module "loader" and the window "viewer".
The window "viewer" uses the module "flattener", the module "distortion" and the module "exporter".
The module "loader" reads the mesh "mesh" from the stl file "model.stl".
The module "loader" uses the library "trimesh".
The window "viewer" uses the library "pyvista".
The module "flattener" uses the library "scipy".
The module "exporter" uses the library "reportlab".
The module "exporter" writes the list "panels" to the svg file "patterns.svg".
The module "exporter" writes the list "panels" to the pdf file "patterns.pdf".
The function "segment_by_seams" converts the mesh "mesh" into the list "face groups".
The function "flatten_patch" uses the function "cut_to_disk" and the algorithm "lscm".
The window "viewer" changes the list "seam_edges".
The window "viewer" changes the stack "seam_segments".

# --- primitives and roles
The algorithm "lscm" follows the method "Levy et al. 2002".
The algorithm "lscm" pins the value "two boundary vertices".
The percentile "angular p95" uses the method "numpy linear interpolation".
The percentile "angular p95" measures the value "angular distortion per face".
The list "panels" has the same unit as the mesh "mesh".
The function "export_pdf" has the unit "mm".
The function "export_svg" has the unit "mm".
The function "export_pdf" reads the list "panels".
The function "export_svg" reads the list "panels".

# --- viewer state machines
The state machine "seam mode" has the states "navigation", "seam without point" and "seam with point".
The state machine "seam mode" starts in the state "navigation".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "seam mode" from the state "navigation" to the state "seam without point".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "seam mode" from the state "seam without point" to the state "seam with point".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "seam mode" from the state "seam with point" to the state "seam without point".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "seam mode" from the state "seam without point" to the state "navigation".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "seam mode" from the state "seam with point" to the state "navigation".
The state machine "distortion mode" has the states "angular", "area" and "none".
The state machine "distortion mode" starts in the state "angular".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "distortion mode" from the state "angular" to the state "area".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "distortion mode" from the state "area" to the state "none".
The window "viewer" moves the state machine "distortion mode" from the state "none" to the state "angular".

# --- invariants
If the mesh "patch" is closed, the function "cut_to_disk" removes the value "last face".
If the algorithm "lscm" raises the error "Exception", the function "flatten_patch" drops the value "panel".
If the list "panels" is empty, the window "viewer" does not call the module "exporter".
If the value "2D area" is less than 0, the function "flatten_patch" flips the value "u axis".
If the stack "seam_segments" is empty, the window "viewer" does not remove the list "seam_edges".
The module "loader" removes the value "degenerate faces" from the mesh "mesh".
